    "result_text": "The build is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `timezone` derived field for owners, sourced from the fixed region-to-timezone table.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `timezone` string property to the `Owner` schema (right after `locality`), so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`CityRegion.java`** \u2014 Added the pinned `REGION_TIMEZONE` map (`NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney`, `VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne`, `QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane`) and a `timezone(String region)` accessor that returns the IANA name, or `null` for an unknown region.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping` for `timezone` that derives it from the same locality used for the existing `locality` field: `CityRegion.timezone(CustomerCode.locality(owner))`. This keeps timezone consistent with the region actually reported (postcode-preferred customerCode region, with city-table fallback).\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsTimezoneForRegion` test (Sydney \u2192 NSW \u2192 `Australia/Sydney`) passes, and the full suite reports `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
